oracle: host CPython 3.11.17, 3.12.3, 3.13.16 (python3.11, python3.12, python3.13)
command: {python3.11,python3.12,python3.13} -I zero_divisor_inside_argument.py
result: exit 1 with ZeroDivisionError on stderr; stdout is exactly the part of <name>.expect before `trap:`
releases: 3.11.17, 3.12.3 and 3.13.16 by their own host interpreters (above); 3.0a1 and 3.16.0a1 through the py3 profile's pinned-source evidence (python-iir-compiler/src/profiles.rs)
why: the argument is evaluated before print writes, so the second call prints nothing
